  "Loops: the loop runs from loopStart (0) to loopEnd, a whole number of bars with the seam crossfade baked in. After loopEnd each file carries a 100 ms post-roll (a copy of the loop head) because decoders differ on Vorbis end trimming, so always set AudioBufferSourceNode.loop = true, loopStart = 0 and loopEnd = loopEnd; never loop the whole buffer. duration = loopEnd; fileSamples includes the post-roll.",
  "The three phase loops are all -16 LUFS integrated, so they crossfade at equal gain.",
  "intro_sting: start it when the intro starts; its deep gong lands at syncTime (1.50 s), the cut to play."
